Lyrics[edit]
The song quotes a line from "You Really Got Me" by the Kinks, with the word "girl" replaced by "boy": "Boy, you really got me goin'/You got me so I don't know what I'm doin'." (For this, Ray Davies received a songwriting credit for "Push It.") It also quotes "Pick up on this" from "I'm a Greedy Man" and "There it is" from "There It Is", both by James Brown. The whispered "Push it" is sampled from the band Coal Kitchen's 1977 recording "Keep on Pushin'". The song is in A minor.&#91;1&#93;

